The physics behind the notes, so you can check it makes sense to you. The maximum displacement is length × beam × depth × water density, which is the weight of water the hull could push aside if it were filled to the brim. If the hull’s own weight is less, it floats, and the difference is the cargo capacity. This treats the hull as a box. You should say that on the site, because real hulls are curved and carry less than a box would.
A couple of things to decide on your own. Is “other environments” in scope? Salt versus fresh is easy, but anything more (waves, temperature) is a stretch for this project. Also, do you want the safe loading checkbox? It gives you a third input type and makes the verdict more realistic, but it’s one more thing to explain.
